@startuml
!include ../../common/eztrade-style.puml

title EZTrade Sequence - Domain Event to WebSocket Notification
autonumber

participant "Domain publisher\nSpring Events" as Events
participant "DomainEventsListener\n@TransactionalEventListener(AFTER_COMMIT)\n@Async" as Listener
participant "NotificationService" as NotificationService
participant "WebSocketNotificationAdapter" as WsAdapter
participant "InboxNotificationAdapter" as InboxAdapter
participant "LoggingEmailNotificationAdapter" as EmailAdapter
participant "LoggingPushNotificationAdapter" as PushAdapter
participant "SimpMessagingTemplate" as Simp
participant "Spring STOMP broker\n/user destination" as Broker
participant "NotificationsWebSocket\nfrontend" as WsClient
participant "Toaster" as Toaster
database "notification_inbox" as InboxDb

Events -> Listener : OrderPlaced / OrderExecuted /\nOrderCancelled / InsufficientFunds /\nPortfolioValuationUpdated
Listener -> NotificationService : handle(event)
NotificationService -> NotificationService : builds NotificationMessage
NotificationService -> EmailAdapter : send(message)
EmailAdapter --> NotificationService : log only
NotificationService -> PushAdapter : send(message)
PushAdapter --> NotificationService : log only
NotificationService -> WsAdapter : send(message)
WsAdapter -> Simp : convertAndSendToUser(recipient,\n/queue/notifications, payload)
Simp -> Broker : route to /user/queue/notifications
Broker -> WsClient : STOMP MESSAGE
WsClient -> Toaster : toast(title, body, variant)
NotificationService -> InboxAdapter : save(message)
InboxAdapter -> InboxDb : insert notification_inbox row

note bottom
Evidence: DomainEventsListener.java, NotificationService.java,
WebSocketNotificationAdapter.java, InboxNotificationAdapter.java, and
frontend/components/notifications/notifications-ws.tsx.
Email and push adapters are logging implementations, not external providers.
end note

@enduml
